WEBVTT

00:00:02.970 --> 00:00:05.720
Come and get it!

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:10.610
He likes it, he likes it!

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:13.260
Yume, is that food...

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:14.110
Don't worry.

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:16.230
I went easy on the sugar!

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:17.480
...so it is sweet.

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:19.460
You like it, don't you, Bunta?

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:22.920
Um, doesn't the fact that it's a calico cat mean it's a girl?

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:23.950
Yup.

00:00:23.950 --> 00:00:26.500
Then we have to think of a girlier name for her.

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:28.240
Let's call her Kana!

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:29.870
Why don't you ask Kana first?

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:31.230
Like she'd ever let you though.

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:33.130
But look!

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:36.640
She totally looks like a Bunta!

00:00:39.590 --> 00:00:42.590
Oh, did the chief already leave?

00:00:42.590 --> 00:00:43.380
Ages ago.

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:46.500
Oh... I thought we were going to go together.

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:48.710
Well, she hasn't been to school in a while.

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:52.110
I bet right now she's doing her best to expand the subscription base.

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:54.140
Expand?

00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:55.680
Blocky birds?

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:57.080
Large intestine?

00:00:57.080 --> 00:00:58.090
Kana.

00:00:58.090 --> 00:00:59.070
Yes?

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:03.130
It's that time already?

00:01:03.130 --> 00:01:04.750
I'm late, I'm late!

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:08.520
I'm late, I'm late!

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:09.580
Kana-chan!

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:10.240
Yes?

00:01:10.610 --> 00:01:15.320
On the days you have school, I'd like bread for breakfast.

00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:17.540
Oh, all right.

00:01:17.540 --> 00:01:19.250
I'm off then.

00:01:19.250 --> 00:01:21.210
Bye.

00:01:24.630 --> 00:01:28.420
This way, she'll be going to school with a piece of bread in her mouth...

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:30.080
I'm late, I'm late!

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:32.480
...and I'll get to see it!

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:34.000
I can't wait!

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:35.550
Stop getting drunk in the morning.

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:40.460
Grandma, today we have a day of summer school,

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:44.180
and it's the first time I'm going to school from work.

00:01:46.930 --> 00:01:49.460
I was worried at first that I might get lost,

00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:54.650
but thanks to the newspaper route, I've even found shortcuts.

00:01:55.440 --> 00:02:00.590
Grandma, I think I'm taking to the newspaper business!

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:37.190
The First Smile

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:33.910
Good morning!

00:03:35.180 --> 00:03:37.200
Good morning!

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:40.380
Ken-kun, you're unbelievable!

00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:46.890
Oh, I wanted to ask you: Where did your mother buy the cakes she gave me?

00:03:46.890 --> 00:03:49.240
Oh, my mom made those herself.

00:03:49.490 --> 00:03:52.700
Oh really? They were so delicious,

00:03:52.700 --> 00:03:56.800
I was sure you must have gotten them from a famous bakery!

00:03:56.800 --> 00:04:00.750
I'll tell my mom you liked them and she'll make them again.

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:02.970
Oh thank you, Ken-kun!

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:06.980
Saki-chan!

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:08.490
Good morning!

00:04:08.490 --> 00:04:12.660
My mom was saying that she'd like to subscribe to your newspaper.

00:04:12.660 --> 00:04:18.090
Really? Then I'll talk to your mom after school!

00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:20.120
Yeah, we could walk home together.

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:20.860
Sure.

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:24.050
Oh, I'll have to ask my mom to subscribe too!

00:04:32.210 --> 00:04:34.360
Good morning everyone!

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:37.120
Just in time!

00:04:37.550 --> 00:04:38.520
Hey Kana...

00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:39.340
What?

00:04:39.770 --> 00:04:41.840
We heard about your grandmother.

00:04:42.690 --> 00:04:44.580
Is there anything we can do for you?

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:46.400
Please tell us if there's anything!

00:04:47.170 --> 00:04:49.190
I will, but...

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:52.000
It's after the bell, folks.

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:53.310
Everyone, please take your seats.

00:04:55.920 --> 00:04:57.790
We'll talk to you later then.

00:04:57.790 --> 00:04:58.450
Okay.

00:04:58.450 --> 00:04:59.510
Keep your chin up!

00:04:59.510 --> 00:05:01.260
Thanks.

00:05:05.890 --> 00:05:08.610
All right everyone, some focus, please!

00:05:09.130 --> 00:05:14.310
This is a special class today, but I'd like to introduce a new student.

00:05:14.310 --> 00:05:18.900
Mika Kujiin will be attending this school from starting this semester.

00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:21.610
Can you please say a few words about yourself to the class?

00:05:24.930 --> 00:05:26.520
Listen up, everyone!

00:05:26.520 --> 00:05:28.640
Let's just say that I'm proof that all men are not created equal!

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:33.450
So I'd have you keep that in mind when addressing me.

00:05:33.970 --> 00:05:36.250
Did you get that, peasants?!

00:05:37.380 --> 00:05:39.050
What is up with this girl?

00:05:39.050 --> 00:05:41.070
Did she really just say that?

00:05:39.830 --> 00:05:41.970
How should I handle this girl?

00:05:41.160 --> 00:05:42.590
I love it!

00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:45.420
I thought it was her.

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:49.730
Oh, you're Kana Nakamachi!

00:05:49.730 --> 00:05:50.930
You actually KNOW her?

00:05:50.930 --> 00:05:52.530
A little.

00:05:52.530 --> 00:05:53.730
Let's leave it at that!

00:05:53.730 --> 00:05:57.160
So really, you just ran into her now and then in your neighborhood.

00:05:57.160 --> 00:06:01.660
Yeah, so she's more like an associate than an acquaintance.

00:06:01.660 --> 00:06:04.190
Associate? But you just ran into her.

00:06:04.190 --> 00:06:05.700
Well, you see...

00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:07.720
Stop spouting nonsense!

00:06:07.720 --> 00:06:11.710
How dare you call yourself my associate!

00:06:11.710 --> 00:06:14.380
So, we're more like friends?

00:06:15.300 --> 00:06:16.790
Fr-Friends?!

00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:18.770
Yup!

00:06:19.110 --> 00:06:23.180
I don't befriend common people.

00:06:23.180 --> 00:06:24.330
Oh.

00:06:24.330 --> 00:06:26.060
Hey,

00:06:26.640 --> 00:06:30.780
isn't your uniform from the White Rose Academy?

00:06:30.780 --> 00:06:33.080
That's such a rich girl school!

00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:34.140
Yeah. So?

00:06:34.140 --> 00:06:37.520
Well, why would you start going to our school,

00:06:37.520 --> 00:06:39.340
if you already went to such a great school?

00:06:39.340 --> 00:06:41.020
Now that you mention it...

00:06:42.550 --> 00:06:44.700
From a ritzy private school,

00:06:45.210 --> 00:06:48.020
to a crummy public one.

00:06:48.490 --> 00:06:49.550
Which means....

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:51.160
I see...

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:55.330
You need to be crazy...?

00:06:51.160 --> 00:06:54.900
Hey, our uniforms are cute, aren't they?

00:06:54.900 --> 00:06:56.280
What?

00:06:56.280 --> 00:06:57.600
Are you mocking me?!

00:06:57.600 --> 00:06:58.970
Not at all!

00:06:58.970 --> 00:07:02.060
Kana, why don't you give her a tour of the school?

00:07:02.970 --> 00:07:07.040
That's right! You probably still don't know where anything is.

00:07:07.040 --> 00:07:11.880
Hah! There's nothing a commoner like you could possibly teach me.

00:07:11.880 --> 00:07:15.270
If anything, I need to take care of you, Kana.

00:07:15.270 --> 00:07:16.920
Go ahead. Ask me anything.

00:07:16.920 --> 00:07:18.220
I really can?

00:07:19.430 --> 00:07:20.610
Uh huh!

00:07:20.610 --> 00:07:21.360
In that case...

00:07:21.360 --> 00:07:22.330
What?

00:07:22.330 --> 00:07:25.230
What was your name again?

00:07:26.290 --> 00:07:28.950
You're so rude!

00:07:29.500 --> 00:07:31.950
We're going shopping.

00:07:31.950 --> 00:07:32.630
Yeah.

00:07:33.050 --> 00:07:36.160
Don't forget the booze I asked for.

00:07:36.160 --> 00:07:38.250
Yeah, yeah.

00:07:43.220 --> 00:07:45.360
I'm home.

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:46.520
Welcome home.

00:07:46.520 --> 00:07:49.980
So, how was your first day back in school?

00:07:49.980 --> 00:07:52.660
Apparently I'm rude.

00:07:52.660 --> 00:07:55.340
You always say the most incomprehensible things...

00:07:55.340 --> 00:07:58.730
and it's so CUTE!

00:08:00.910 --> 00:08:03.110
Stop making everything perverted!

00:08:03.110 --> 00:08:07.860
Fine, I get it. Then just once!

00:08:07.860 --> 00:08:09.400
Didn't you say "Fine"?!

00:08:09.400 --> 00:08:12.260
It's just the last eight times, just the last eight!

00:08:12.260 --> 00:08:14.370
You're counting up!

00:08:12.260 --> 00:08:14.380
I said it's only eight more!

00:08:14.680 --> 00:08:18.010
Just four more! Five is fine too, five is fine!

00:08:18.380 --> 00:08:20.530
What are you guys doing?

00:08:20.530 --> 00:08:22.680
What do you mean? This is normal.

00:08:22.680 --> 00:08:24.280
That's not what I'm talking about.

00:08:24.280 --> 00:08:28.090
I'm asking why you're doing it when the door is open!

00:08:28.090 --> 00:08:32.140
If word gets around that we're harboring a pervert here,
 it'll affect our subscriptions.

00:08:32.140 --> 00:08:33.170
So, how'd it go, anyway?

00:08:33.170 --> 00:08:35.060
Get a good crop?

00:08:35.060 --> 00:08:37.050
Of course!

00:08:37.050 --> 00:08:38.750
I wasn't expecting anything less!

00:08:38.750 --> 00:08:40.630
Good job, chief.

00:08:40.630 --> 00:08:46.290
What exactly did you mean this morning, when you were talking about expansion?

00:08:47.550 --> 00:08:49.600
How to explain it...

00:08:49.600 --> 00:08:51.650
It's subscriptions.

00:08:51.650 --> 00:08:56.850
What? You mean, for the newspaper?

00:08:56.850 --> 00:09:00.510
You think I'm thinking about any other kind?

00:09:00.960 --> 00:09:03.700
But these are grade-school kids...

00:09:03.700 --> 00:09:07.890
Yeah, and they all live in this neighborhood, right?

00:09:09.240 --> 00:09:13.030
If you get friendly with the kids, 
you can get friendly with their parents.

00:09:13.030 --> 00:09:15.610
Then it's easy to get new subscribers.

00:09:15.610 --> 00:09:17.890
I didn't know you went that far.

00:09:17.890 --> 00:09:19.610
That's just basic stuff.

00:09:19.610 --> 00:09:25.050
And now that you're here,
 you too will master the perfect expansion smile.

00:09:25.050 --> 00:09:26.840
Expansion smile?

00:09:26.840 --> 00:09:27.670
That's right.

00:09:27.670 --> 00:09:29.490
Take a good look.

00:09:30.200 --> 00:09:31.740
Like this!

00:09:32.710 --> 00:09:33.910
Wow...

00:09:36.550 --> 00:09:38.180
Now do it.

00:09:38.680 --> 00:09:39.730
Okay.

00:09:42.630 --> 00:09:44.520
Here I go!

00:09:43.280 --> 00:09:45.690
Where are my glasses?

00:09:45.690 --> 00:09:47.210
Smile!

00:09:47.210 --> 00:09:48.690
Huh?

00:09:52.040 --> 00:09:56.500
Wow, how should I put it?

00:09:56.500 --> 00:09:58.920
Sorry, I shouldn't have pushed you.

00:09:58.920 --> 00:10:03.980
No, I'm useless! Useless!!!

00:10:17.010 --> 00:10:20.290
Would this work?

00:10:20.290 --> 00:10:21.400
Or this...

00:10:21.400 --> 00:10:22.280
Kana?

00:10:22.280 --> 00:10:23.320
Yes?

00:10:23.990 --> 00:10:26.290
I really can't do it!

00:10:26.290 --> 00:10:29.070
What am I doing wrong?

00:10:29.070 --> 00:10:30.790
Let me put it this way.

00:10:30.790 --> 00:10:34.000
This is a normal smile.

00:10:32.840 --> 00:10:34.340
Smile

00:10:34.350 --> 00:10:38.010
Niboraspon 
Slimy

00:10:35.060 --> 00:10:36.320
And this is your smile.

00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:38.520
What is "Niboraspon" and "Slimy" supposed to mean?!

00:10:38.520 --> 00:10:42.110
Well, I'm sure you can improve with practice.

00:10:42.110 --> 00:10:45.960
So Kana, don't cry in earnest, okay?

00:10:45.960 --> 00:10:47.280
All right.

00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:50.370
So I have to practice more...

00:10:50.370 --> 00:10:52.000
Who's there?

00:10:52.600 --> 00:10:54.570
Is that you, Kujiin-san?

00:10:58.140 --> 00:11:00.360
Oh, it's you, Kana.

00:11:00.360 --> 00:11:03.040
What's wrong? Did you get lost again?

00:11:03.040 --> 00:11:05.050
As if I would ever get lost, you rude thing!

00:11:05.050 --> 00:11:07.020
Excuse me!

00:11:07.020 --> 00:11:08.890
Then what are you doing here?

00:11:08.890 --> 00:11:11.160
Well... I...

00:11:11.160 --> 00:11:14.380
I just happened to be in the neighborhood.

00:11:14.380 --> 00:11:15.670
You don't say.

00:11:15.670 --> 00:11:17.520
Kana, who is that?

00:11:17.520 --> 00:11:18.860
Is she a customer?

00:11:18.860 --> 00:11:21.600
This is Mika Kujiin...

00:11:21.600 --> 00:11:22.520
Oh...

00:11:22.520 --> 00:11:23.310
From the Kajitsu Times.

00:11:23.310 --> 00:11:25.050
The Kajitsu Times?!

00:11:25.050 --> 00:11:29.040
You're a spy for the Kajitsu Times!

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:31.690
What are you talking about?

00:11:31.690 --> 00:11:34.230
I came by here after working on expanding the Kajitsu's readership.

00:11:34.230 --> 00:11:37.200
Expanding, you say?!

00:11:37.200 --> 00:11:39.270
It's about the newspaper's subscriber base.

00:11:39.270 --> 00:11:40.810
I know what she's doing!

00:11:40.810 --> 00:11:43.280
Anyway, come with me!

00:11:44.060 --> 00:11:47.030
Kujiin-san, can you wait there for a moment?

00:11:47.610 --> 00:11:49.150
What's wrong?

00:11:49.150 --> 00:11:51.320
Listen up, Kana.

00:11:51.320 --> 00:11:54.650
We lost 15 subscribers last month to the Kajitsu Times!

00:11:54.650 --> 00:11:56.790
And when I asked why they switched to the Kajitsu,

00:11:56.790 --> 00:11:58.250
you know what they said?

00:11:57.900 --> 00:12:03.680
Rice.

00:11:58.250 --> 00:11:59.980
Rice!

00:11:59.980 --> 00:12:03.690
Apparently, they give you rice if you subscribe with them!

00:12:03.690 --> 00:12:05.600
So, what the heck is up with that?!

00:12:05.600 --> 00:12:09.190
We're not in the rice business, we're in the newspaper business!

00:12:09.190 --> 00:12:13.230
If you don't have rice, why don't you eat paper?!

00:12:11.320 --> 00:12:13.230
Chief! Please calm down!

00:12:13.230 --> 00:12:15.310
Which is why, Kana.

00:12:15.310 --> 00:12:16.680
Yes?

00:12:16.680 --> 00:12:18.230
I want you to go, too.

00:12:18.230 --> 00:12:19.620
Where am I going?

00:12:20.230 --> 00:12:22.870
Subscriber hunting!

00:12:35.870 --> 00:12:39.980
It's such a coincidence that you're subscriber hunting, too.

00:12:39.980 --> 00:12:41.890
Not really. My boss told me to.

00:12:42.830 --> 00:12:46.500
I want you to go subscriber hunting with her.

00:12:46.500 --> 00:12:48.760
You'll go with her and smile.

00:12:48.760 --> 00:12:49.670
Got it?

00:12:49.670 --> 00:12:51.320
Yes, Chief.

00:12:51.320 --> 00:12:54.100
But my smile isn't exactly charming.

00:12:54.100 --> 00:12:56.950
Yes. Your smile will be a powerful weapon.

00:12:56.950 --> 00:13:00.540
What do you mean?

00:13:00.540 --> 00:13:02.890
I thought I had a horrible smile.

00:13:02.890 --> 00:13:07.810
No. Your smile is wonderful!

00:13:08.430 --> 00:13:10.000
It is?

00:13:11.420 --> 00:13:13.850
Then I'm not hopeless?

00:13:13.850 --> 00:13:14.720
Of course not!

00:13:14.720 --> 00:13:16.950
So go out there and get 'em!

00:13:16.950 --> 00:13:18.270
Yes, Chief!

00:13:18.660 --> 00:13:22.450
So what, you're going to the same places as me?

00:13:22.450 --> 00:13:23.650
Yes.

00:13:23.650 --> 00:13:25.340
I see.

00:13:25.340 --> 00:13:28.220
So I guess subscriber hunting is something

00:13:28.220 --> 00:13:29.930
you do with people from other newspapers.

00:13:29.930 --> 00:13:31.270
It looks like it.

00:13:34.140 --> 00:13:35.410
Here I go.

00:13:41.290 --> 00:13:42.090
Yes?

00:13:42.090 --> 00:13:44.840
May I interest you in a subscription to the Kajitsu Times?

00:13:44.840 --> 00:13:48.880
It's not going to work; this person is a foreigner!

00:13:48.880 --> 00:13:51.430
Oh, the Kajitsu newspaper?

00:13:51.430 --> 00:13:53.020
He understood you?

00:13:53.020 --> 00:13:55.390
All right, now it's my turn.

00:13:55.690 --> 00:13:58.850
Um... I'm from the Fuushin Gazette.

00:13:58.850 --> 00:14:00.610
Would you like to sign up?

00:14:05.380 --> 00:14:06.750
What was wrong with him?

00:14:08.040 --> 00:14:09.810
Oh well, next!

00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:15.160
Yes?

00:14:15.160 --> 00:14:16.540
I'm here from the Kajitsu Times...

00:14:16.540 --> 00:14:18.980
...and I'm here from the Fuushin Gazette.

00:14:18.980 --> 00:14:20.630
Can we interest you in a subscription?

00:14:25.500 --> 00:14:27.790
Kujiin-san... I think...

00:14:32.420 --> 00:14:34.590
We're not quitting!

00:14:36.750 --> 00:14:38.140
Next!

00:14:43.680 --> 00:14:45.910
Next!

00:14:51.700 --> 00:14:53.560
I guess I'll have

00:14:53.560 --> 00:14:55.650
to have Haruka go around and pick up

00:14:55.650 --> 00:14:57.950
all the potential subscribers that got scared away.

00:15:04.760 --> 00:15:07.220
That was a total failure.

00:15:08.260 --> 00:15:10.550
I wonder why.

00:15:10.550 --> 00:15:12.680
I was going to ask you the same question.

00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:14.180
But thinking about it,

00:15:14.180 --> 00:15:15.740
it's almost as if they closed the door

00:15:15.740 --> 00:15:17.870
whenever they looked at your face.

00:15:18.610 --> 00:15:21.720
No, I knew it wouldn't work!

00:15:21.720 --> 00:15:25.560
But the chief told me I had such a wonderful smile.

00:15:25.560 --> 00:15:28.760
Yet somehow, as soon as they saw my face, people shut their doors.

00:15:28.760 --> 00:15:31.970
Wait a minute... does that mean...

00:15:31.970 --> 00:15:35.710
You talk too much!

00:15:35.710 --> 00:15:39.920
Just show me that smile already.

00:15:40.160 --> 00:15:43.260
Huh? Oh, well...

00:15:43.800 --> 00:15:46.070
Here goes.

00:15:54.350 --> 00:15:56.220
How was it?

00:15:56.220 --> 00:15:58.320
There's no word other than bad...

00:15:58.320 --> 00:16:01.790
You're right, it's bad. I knew it...

00:16:00.560 --> 00:16:02.410
Kana?

00:16:02.410 --> 00:16:04.380
But... but...

00:16:04.700 --> 00:16:09.360
Then fix it already, if it's bad!

00:16:10.160 --> 00:16:13.630
You just need to practice smiling!

00:16:13.970 --> 00:16:16.200
Kurin-san?

00:16:18.550 --> 00:16:19.900
I guess you're right.

00:16:19.900 --> 00:16:22.240
Chief also said I could get better if I practiced.

00:16:22.240 --> 00:16:23.540
That's right.

00:16:23.540 --> 00:16:27.650
Well, if you want I could help you practice.

00:16:27.650 --> 00:16:28.640
Really?

00:16:28.640 --> 00:16:30.470
I told you I'd take care of you!

00:16:31.280 --> 00:16:33.960
Oh, thank you, Mika-chan!

00:16:36.300 --> 00:16:39.910
Mika-chan??!

00:16:40.760 --> 00:16:42.210
You fool!

00:16:42.210 --> 00:16:44.490
I didn't give you permission for that!

00:16:44.490 --> 00:16:49.560
I'm sorry, Mi... I mean, Kujiin-san. I just...

00:16:53.220 --> 00:16:55.810
You're doing it wrong. It's not like that.

00:16:56.440 --> 00:16:57.740
Like this!

00:16:59.470 --> 00:17:00.500
What?

00:17:00.500 --> 00:17:02.740
Nothing, I was just thinking you had a very nice smile.

00:17:02.740 --> 00:17:04.860
Well, DUH.

00:17:04.860 --> 00:17:06.930
Try again!

00:17:06.930 --> 00:17:08.990
Okay. How about this?

00:17:08.990 --> 00:17:11.160
You're narrowing your eyes too much.

00:17:11.160 --> 00:17:12.500
Or this?

00:17:12.500 --> 00:17:14.270
Now you're bugging them out!

00:17:14.680 --> 00:17:15.680
What about now?

00:17:15.680 --> 00:17:16.670
NO!

00:17:16.670 --> 00:17:18.110
Or now?

00:17:18.110 --> 00:17:20.780
You look like you're in agony.

00:17:21.390 --> 00:17:24.170
Here kitty!

00:17:26.520 --> 00:17:28.510
Why?

00:17:30.530 --> 00:17:33.880
I wonder what exactly is wrong.

00:17:33.880 --> 00:17:37.730
I don't know what to do.

00:17:39.820 --> 00:17:42.180
I think you're too stiff.

00:17:42.730 --> 00:17:45.260
Stop moving around!

00:17:45.260 --> 00:17:48.150
Kujiin-san, that tickles.

00:17:48.150 --> 00:17:50.110
I said don't move!

00:17:56.550 --> 00:17:58.040
Hmm...

00:17:59.030 --> 00:18:00.840
I guess that's all right.

00:18:00.840 --> 00:18:01.840
Really?

00:18:01.840 --> 00:18:03.840
At least it's not scary anymore.

00:18:05.110 --> 00:18:09.080
I did it! Yay, yay!

00:18:13.240 --> 00:18:15.990
Now, let's put it to the test!

00:18:20.120 --> 00:18:21.570
I guess they're not home...

00:18:24.440 --> 00:18:25.550
What the...?

00:18:25.550 --> 00:18:27.970
No, their electricity meter is clocking fast.

00:18:27.970 --> 00:18:29.700
They must be pretending to not be home.

00:18:30.500 --> 00:18:32.700
Unbelievable! How dare they!

00:18:34.170 --> 00:18:37.780
No, if you do that, you're going to make them angry!

00:18:37.780 --> 00:18:39.600
Well, what should we do then?

00:18:39.600 --> 00:18:41.750
Well...

00:18:41.750 --> 00:18:43.970
This is taking too long.

00:18:43.970 --> 00:18:45.250
In that case...

00:18:46.780 --> 00:18:49.230
FIRE!

00:18:49.230 --> 00:18:50.590
Did someone say, "fire"?

00:18:50.590 --> 00:18:51.440
Is there a fire?

00:18:51.440 --> 00:18:52.280
Fire?!

00:18:52.280 --> 00:18:53.610
Where's the fire?!

00:18:54.920 --> 00:18:57.050
Actually, there is no....

00:18:57.050 --> 00:19:00.050
I'm sorry!!!

00:19:00.050 --> 00:19:01.970
So?

00:19:06.500 --> 00:19:07.920
That was scary.

00:19:07.920 --> 00:19:09.670
What are you talking about?

00:19:09.670 --> 00:19:12.410
That was your big chance, and you let it slip away!

00:19:12.410 --> 00:19:16.420
It was a chance for you to put your practice to the test and show your smile!

00:19:17.040 --> 00:19:18.990
I'm sorry

00:19:18.990 --> 00:19:23.980
for letting that opportunity go, 
when you took the trouble to give me a chance.

00:19:23.980 --> 00:19:25.950
What are you talking about?

00:19:25.950 --> 00:19:28.110
I would never do something for you!

00:19:29.500 --> 00:19:31.160
It's already eight.

00:19:31.160 --> 00:19:32.620
You're right.

00:19:32.620 --> 00:19:36.720
If I don't get home soon, everyone's going to worry.

00:19:36.720 --> 00:19:37.900
Me too.

00:19:37.900 --> 00:19:39.610
I'll see you later then.

00:19:39.610 --> 00:19:41.320
Hey, Kana!

00:19:41.650 --> 00:19:42.650
Huh?

00:19:42.650 --> 00:19:46.230
Well... just...

00:19:51.550 --> 00:19:56.990
Kana, from now on, you may call me by my first name!

00:19:56.990 --> 00:19:58.170
Really?

00:19:58.170 --> 00:20:01.090
Of course. For I am kind.

00:20:01.390 --> 00:20:04.140
All right, Mika-chan!

00:20:05.700 --> 00:20:07.090
See you later!

00:20:14.720 --> 00:20:18.810
Kana's smile has really gotten good.

00:20:27.180 --> 00:20:30.880
I practiced my smile today.

00:20:30.880 --> 00:20:32.430
You practiced...

00:20:32.430 --> 00:20:33.700
...your smile?

00:20:35.200 --> 00:20:40.660
Yeah well, Kana's business smile was pretty darn freaky.

00:20:40.660 --> 00:20:42.260
You're horrible!

00:20:42.260 --> 00:20:44.500
Don't cry, Kana-chan!

00:20:45.940 --> 00:20:49.140
I'm sorry Kana. When I said "pretty darn freaky,"
 I was talking about this person.

00:20:49.140 --> 00:20:51.080
No, it's fine.

00:20:51.950 --> 00:20:55.680
You see, I practiced to get better.

00:20:55.680 --> 00:20:59.670
Show it here, then.

00:20:59.670 --> 00:21:02.960
Okay, here I go!

00:21:12.050 --> 00:21:13.810
Smile!

00:21:18.630 --> 00:21:21.890
No! It's still weird, isn't it?!

00:21:22.430 --> 00:21:27.180
No, no, it's a lot better than what you had earlier.

00:21:27.180 --> 00:21:28.360
Really?

00:21:28.680 --> 00:21:32.320
Anyway, what was that face again?

00:21:32.320 --> 00:21:33.680
Smile!

00:21:34.650 --> 00:21:36.830
It's gotten pretty good!

00:21:36.830 --> 00:21:41.180
You really are too cute.

00:21:53.560 --> 00:21:59.970
I'm having so much fun with everyone, grandma!

00:23:30.870 --> 00:23:33.300
The next episode will be "My First Time at the Pool".

00:23:33.300 --> 00:23:34.250
And now, let's play a word game.

00:23:34.250 --> 00:23:35.940
Sweet stuff only!

00:23:35.940 --> 00:23:37.390
Yogurt.

00:23:37.390 --> 00:23:38.740
Truffles.

00:23:38.740 --> 00:23:40.150
Skittles.

00:23:40.150 --> 00:23:42.040
Salty caramel.
